<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Scotland</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Scottish</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Scotland is a country occupying the northern part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain">Great Britain</a>. Roman forces campaigned there but never fully conquered it, as accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> note. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acts-of-union-1707">Acts of Union</a> of 1707 united Scotland and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> into the Kingdom of Great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, and accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> treat the union as combining Scottish commercial energy with English colonial access.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/scotland.jpg" alt="Scotland" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: none known · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Scotland.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
